</figure>
<div id="S5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To understand contribution of components of <span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif">BlockRank</span> (RQ3), we perform several ablation experiments, primarily on the MSMarco dataset with <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=50</annotation></semantics></math>. More ablation is provided in Section <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Additional Results ‣ Scalable In-context Ranking with Generative Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a> of Appendix.</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Impact of Training Loss</h4>

<div id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S5.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 5.3 Ablation Studies ‣ 5 Experimental Results ‣ Scalable In-context Ranking with Generative Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> ablates the contributions of <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{NTP}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{NTP}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{aux}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{aux}</annotation></semantics></math> to P@1, evaluated with both auto-regressive and attention-based inference.
Introducing <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{aux}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{aux}</annotation></semantics></math> consistently enhances performance for attention-based inference, and for <span id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif">BlockRank</span> (which incorporates structured attention), it increases from 27.8 to 29.1.
As expected, the <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{NTP}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{NTP}</annotation></semantics></math> objective is crucial for generative decoding performance, as seen by the sharp drop in Decode Prec@1 for ‘<span id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif">BlockRank</span> (w/o ntp)’ to 15.8. Notably, the full <span id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif">BlockRank</span> configuration achieves the highest Attn Prec@1 (29.1), demonstrating that <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{aux}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{aux}</annotation></semantics></math> effectively optimizes attention scores for direct retrieval, making attention-based inference the preferred mode for our method.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T4" class="ltx_table ltx_align_floatright" style="width:50%;">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>Ablation: Inference Method Effectiveness &amp; Latency (MSMarco, N=50).</figcaption><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S5.T4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="111.37" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 238.69 111.37" width="238.69"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,111.37) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.32 L 0 106.05 C 0 108.99 2.38 111.37 5.32 111.37 L 233.37 111.37 C 236.31 111.37 238.69 108.99 238.69 106.05 L 238.69 5.32 C 238.69 2.38 236.31 0 233.37 0 L 5.32 0 C 2.38 0 0 2.38 0 5.32 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FCFCFF;" fill="#FCFCFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.38 5.32 L 1.38 106.05 C 1.38 108.23 3.15 109.99 5.32 109.99 L 233.37 109.99 C 235.54 109.99 237.3 108.23 237.3 106.05 L 237.3 5.32 C 237.3 3.15 235.54 1.38 233.37 1.38 L 5.32 1.38 C 3.15 1.38 1.38 3.15 1.38 5.32 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 9.26 52.23)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:14.32em;--ltx-fo-height:3.89em;--ltx-fo-depth:3.39em;font-size:10pt;" class="ltx_minipage" height="100.73" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 53.83)" width="15.91em"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
